course: dictionary
lesson: 7339
title: One word, three meanings: plasma
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Blood is a yellowish liquid called plasma carrying red cells, white cells and platelets.» Here the words blood and liquid are your clues, so plasma is the liquid part of blood.
explain: The same word can point somewhere completely different. «Lightning and glowing signs contain plasma, a fourth state: gas so hot or charged that its atoms lose electrons.» Lightning and signs are not liquids, so this plasma is a state of matter, not something inside blood.
explain: Read the words next to the word and ask which meaning fits. «She bought a new plasma for the lounge.» Your home clues are lounge and a screen, so plasma here is a flat-screen television. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Plasma is the pale yellow liquid part of blood. It carries blood cells, food and waste around the body.
fact: Plasma is about 55% of blood, and people can donate plasma.
fact: In physics, plasma is the fourth state of matter, after solid, liquid and gas.
fact: Plasma is a very hot gas whose particles have an electric charge, as in «lightning» and «neon signs».
fact: Stars are made mostly of plasma. A plasma TV is a kind of flat-screen television.
exercise: «Blood is a yellowish liquid called plasma carrying red cells, white cells and platelets.» What is plasma in this sentence? | A kind of flat-screen television | A very hot gas in the Sun | *The pale yellow liquid part of blood | A small red cell
exercise: «Lightning and glowing signs contain plasma, a fourth state: gas so hot or charged that its atoms lose electrons.» Which state of matter is plasma? | Ice | Solid | Liquid | *A fourth state: a very hot gas with charged particles
exercise: «She bought a new plasma for the lounge, and it shows the football in bright colours.» What is a plasma here? | A small drop of liquid | A blood cell | *A flat-screen television | A star
test: Scientists say stars are made mostly of what? | Solid rock | Red blood cells | *Plasma | Liquid water
test: About how much of blood is plasma? | About 10% | *About 55% | All of it | About 90%
exam: In «People can donate plasma», which meaning of plasma fits best? | A flat-screen television | A cell in a star | *The pale yellow liquid part of blood | A fourth state of matter, like lightning
